If the syntax does not match, meaningful error messages are generated to help the user correct their input.

\subsection{Semantic Analysis}
The semantic analyzer processes the validated tokens to extract meaningful musical data. Each instruction is transformed into a tuple \texttt{(note, duration, time)}. This structured data is used by the visualizer to render the final piano roll. The semantic phase also handles validation of values (e.g., ensuring durations are positive).

\subsection{Visualization}
Once semantic data is extracted, the system uses \texttt{matplotlib} to create a piano roll. Each note is displayed as a horizontal bar positioned by its pitch and start time, with length proportional to its duration.

